"result\" each being list of floats (or numbers). Use only standard library. Do not mutate case.\n\nImplementation details: iterate over matrix rows, compute weighted sums, then compute result with nested loops or list comprehensions. Use float for computations.\n\nPotential floating point precision: use Python floats.\n\nEdge cases: matrix could be any size? Probably always list of lists of ints (0/1). idf and vector are lists of floats.\n\nWrite code:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    M = case['matrix']\n    idf = case['idf']\n    vec = case['vector']\n    n_docs = len(M)\n    n_terms = len(idf)\n    W = [[M[i][j] * idf[j] for j in range(n_terms)] for i in range(n_docs)]\n    degree = [sum(W[i]) for i in range(n_docs)]\n    result = [sum(W[i][j] * vec[i] for i in range(n_docs)) for j in range(n_terms)]\n    return {'degree': degree, 'result': result}\n\nBe careful: result must be list of numbers, could be floats. Use float multiplication.\n\nNow output as JSON with key \"implementation\". The whole response must be a JSON object with single key \"implementation\". The value must be a JSON string containing the Python source code, with proper escaping.\n\nWe'll produce the JSON.\n\nMake sure to include no extra text, just the JSON object.\n\nLet's write the final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1357,"completion_tokens":3113,"total_tokens":4470,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1280},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2956},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1280,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":77},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}